WEBVTT

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:13.990
October 20th 3:05 AM

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.030
Irina...

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.990
Parachute Training Facility - Parachute Tower

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.910
I'm fine. This is nothing.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:20.960
You sure about that?

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:22.460
Don't make fun!

00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:32.260
It's been ten days
since Irina started training.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.900
Her performance in practically all of the
training rivaled the finest candidates.

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:53.030
The only exception... being this.

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:54.370
Need a hand?

00:00:54.370 --> 00:00:57.290
No need. It's just...

00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:06.090
I'm imagining what it'll look like
when I crash full speed into the ground.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.170
We've gotta fix that.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:35.360
Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:50.900
Night Flight

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.980
October 21st 2:00 PM

00:02:51.610 --> 00:02:56.030
The capital of Zirnitra Union, Sangrad.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:56.360
Sangrad - Citadel

00:02:56.030 --> 00:03:04.290
Within the massive walls of its Citadel,
a secret cabinet meeting was being held.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.240
Cabinet Meeting

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:12.420
Currently, experiment subject
N44 is strong and healthy.

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:18.430
Training is going well. We believe she's
capable of handling the test flight.

00:03:18.430 --> 00:03:24.470
I see, I see! Comrade Chief,
is the unit progressing well?

00:03:24.470 --> 00:03:31.770
Yes. Assuming all goes well with N44,
final tests will conclude next March.

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:35.570
Then, plan for the real deal in April.

00:03:41.030 --> 00:03:45.620
Now, regarding the subject's
handling post-experiment--

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.500
Execution!

00:03:47.500 --> 00:03:55.710
Until our human flight is complete, it's
necessary to study space's after-effects.

00:03:55.710 --> 00:04:02.470
But afterward, she need not live! Once her
part is done, we should dispose of her!

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:11.690
Launch is yet far off, so there's
no need to make any firm decisions.

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.690
They're difficult to go back on later.

00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:24.410
Damn those old-fashioned dinosaurs!

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:24.490
Gergiev's Office

00:04:29.370 --> 00:04:33.710
I've had to do one
damn purge after another!

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:37.340
How much manpower
must they make me waste?!

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:43.680
In that case, just find a reason
to send them to prison camp.

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:42.840
Gergiev's Aide - Press Secretary
Lyudmila Kharlova

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.510
It's man's first spaceflight--
a feat which will prove

00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:52.480
we're the world's foremost superpower!

00:04:52.480 --> 00:04:55.150
And yet, these goons!

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.400
Mmm. So sweet.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:05:06.620
These days, getting ahead in spaceflight
may be a more potent weapon than nukes.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:11.410
Yes, perhaps. But in order
to outwit everyone,

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.540
we must think how to utilize
our secret ingredient--

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:21.130
"N44," the vampire, Irina Luminesk.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:23.800
October 23rd 11:25 AM

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:26.380
Space Research City 'Laika44' - Streets

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.850
Lev. Are you off-duty today?

00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:35.020
Yeah.

00:05:35.020 --> 00:05:38.730
Poor dude's gotta watch
a monster every day!

00:05:38.730 --> 00:05:42.900
How are things going
with the experiment subject?

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.910
Irina-- She's been exceptional.
Training has gone... really well.

00:05:49.950 --> 00:05:52.660
She can hold her own
against us candidates--

00:05:52.660 --> 00:05:55.130
Don't group us with her.

00:05:55.130 --> 00:06:00.010
She's just an experiment
so we can make it to space.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:03.760
Besides, you're no longer a candidate.

00:06:03.760 --> 00:06:09.600
Though, if you ask me, it's nice
that a top candidate got demoted.

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:10.520
Quit it.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:15.230
There's just one pilot and we've
already got Mikhail and Roza.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:20.690
If you were in the race, too,
there'd be no chance for the rest of us!

00:06:20.690 --> 00:06:25.660
I've never been more thankful
for your short temper!

00:06:25.660 --> 00:06:28.330
Sorry to bug you, Lev.

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:34.000
To be honest, some among us
don't look kindly upon N44.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.790
After all, nobody in history
has gone to space before.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:43.800
And although she's an experiment,
she'll be the first one to do so.

00:06:43.800 --> 00:06:44.970
Mikhail!

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:46.510
Yeah! I'm coming.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:52.600
"No longer a candidate," huh?

00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.600
Training Center - Exam Room

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:04.030
I guess you've lost a little weight.
Is training tough?

00:07:04.030 --> 00:07:05.450
Not really.

00:07:05.450 --> 00:07:10.160
Then I'll have to ask Natalia
to whip up a new menu.

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:12.370
Any other concerns?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:13.620
Nope.

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:14.490
Irinyan!

00:07:14.490 --> 00:07:15.750
Huh?

00:07:15.750 --> 00:07:19.500
Do you mind if I call you that?

00:07:19.500 --> 00:07:25.340
I'm not a candidate,
so their rules don't apply to me!

00:07:25.340 --> 00:07:28.510
In return, you can call me Anya!

00:07:32.350 --> 00:07:33.930
Suit yourself.

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.890
Thanks, Irinyan!

00:07:37.810 --> 00:07:38.470
Aren't you--

00:07:38.470 --> 00:07:40.980
Anya.

00:07:40.980 --> 00:07:42.400
Anya!

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:48.030
Anya, aren't you afraid of me?

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.360
What?

00:07:49.360 --> 00:07:52.950
Even knowing the
cursed species thing is a lie,

00:07:52.950 --> 00:07:57.460
there are plenty of humans
who fear and loathe us.

00:07:57.460 --> 00:08:04.050
I'm a researcher, Irinyan.
I couldn't do my job if I feared you.

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:09.380
Understanding something
is the best way to beat your fear of it.

00:08:09.380 --> 00:08:14.810
Besides, Irinyan is super cute! Oh, yeah!

00:08:14.810 --> 00:08:19.440
Soda water! You like
lemon seltzer, don't you?!

00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.520
How do you know?

00:08:20.520 --> 00:08:22.190
Lev told me!

00:08:22.190 --> 00:08:28.650
So you don't have taste, but you
make up for it with texture and smell?!

00:08:28.650 --> 00:08:30.530
I'm very intrigued!

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.990
He had to open his mouth...

00:08:36.700 --> 00:08:38.580
Jazz Bar 'Zvezda'

00:08:48.550 --> 00:08:51.130
Training has gone... really well.

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:53.140
I said that, but...

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:55.180
<i>Textbook of Psychiatry</i>

00:08:56.810 --> 00:09:01.560
"Fear of heights is
a normal animal instinct.

00:08:56.890 --> 00:08:58.850
<i>Overcoming Acrophobia</i>

00:09:01.560 --> 00:09:06.480
However, the period of fear
is short at under 30 minutes

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:09.320
and will gradually diminish.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:17.490
With repetitive exposure to heights,
it may resolve the fear in the patient."

00:09:18.700 --> 00:09:21.330
I've gotta do something.

00:09:21.330 --> 00:09:27.460
If she's seen as a poor choice
for the flight, she'll be killed for sure.

00:09:27.460 --> 00:09:33.130
Our motherland doesn't know the word
"failure." Only "accidents" and "purges."

00:09:33.130 --> 00:09:40.480
Experiment subject N44, Irina Luminesk,
won't be remembered in space's history.

00:09:44.310 --> 00:09:48.280
Soaring through the sky
is so beautiful, too.

00:09:48.280 --> 00:09:50.440
If only Irina knew.

00:09:51.740 --> 00:09:54.240
That's it! If only she knew!

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:02.990
IRINA: THE VAMPIRE COSMONAUT

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:06.000
October 25th 1:07 AM

00:10:06.710 --> 00:10:13.170
Today, we'll be doing special training
to overcome your acrophobia.

00:10:13.170 --> 00:10:16.760
Your wild imagination
is only making it worse.

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.140
So? What's the plan?

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:22.560
Some drastic measures--flying!

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:25.020
Huh? Flying?

00:10:27.640 --> 00:10:29.650
Military Airfield

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.190
We're here.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:44.830
Here we go!

00:11:11.650 --> 00:11:15.280
We'll keep going up
till we're above the clouds!

00:11:20.910 --> 00:11:22.540
Open your eyes!

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:24.330
I'm trying!

00:11:41.100 --> 00:11:48.810
The first time I flew, it felt like I had
wings! It changed my outlook on life!

00:11:48.810 --> 00:11:52.900
Here's hoping you feel
freedom now, not fear!

00:12:00.820 --> 00:12:02.240
Freedom...

00:12:32.650 --> 00:12:38.030
Welcome to the boundary
of land and space! You all right?!

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:40.860
Yeah, I'm good!

00:12:40.860 --> 00:12:44.740
When will I go beyond this sky?

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.540
Hey, Irina.

00:12:49.540 --> 00:12:51.290
What?

00:12:51.290 --> 00:12:54.710
Uh, never mind.

00:12:57.010 --> 00:12:59.800
Isn't your homeland just over there?

00:13:01.840 --> 00:13:03.850
Wanna closer look?

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:08.100
No, let's go back. The sun's coming up.

00:13:20.030 --> 00:13:21.860
Thanks.

00:13:21.860 --> 00:13:23.200
Huh?!

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:26.120
I'm not afraid anymore!

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:29.000
That's good! That's real good!

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:32.080
Good, good!

00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.380
Dummy.

00:13:54.810 --> 00:13:57.320
That's blood for emergencies.

00:13:59.610 --> 00:14:01.070
What happened?!

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:05.570
An accident at Albinar!
A few engineers got hurt!

00:14:05.570 --> 00:14:07.200
Albinar?

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:10.950
It's a base that launches
rockets and satellites.

00:14:12.290 --> 00:14:17.380
So much panic.
Was it really just a few people?

00:14:21.420 --> 00:14:25.840
An ICBM had exploded during a test launch.

00:14:25.840 --> 00:14:30.140
That's what truly happened at Albinar.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:34.900
Over 500 people were
killed in the accident.

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:37.810
However, it was covered up.

00:14:37.810 --> 00:14:42.150
Publicly, they announced
it had been an airplane accident.

00:14:42.150 --> 00:14:51.080
But within the government, there was talk
that it had been part of someone's scheme.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:56.830
October 27th 1:22 AM

00:14:54.660 --> 00:15:00.920
The night flight seemed to largely
remedy Irina's fear of heights.

00:14:56.830 --> 00:14:59.830
80m Drop Training Tower

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:04.800
Her training was progressing, but...

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:13.390
Five-point landing!
Feet, calves, thighs, hips, back!

00:15:18.730 --> 00:15:21.440
Ouch.

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:23.570
I hit my nose!

00:15:25.530 --> 00:15:30.700
Still, you've gotten a bit better.
Let's take a break.

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:39.710
It's nice that they gave us soda water.

00:15:39.710 --> 00:15:46.380
What about the Albinar accident?
Did it interrupt the plans?

00:15:46.380 --> 00:15:52.260
In a few days, they'll have someone
new in charge to get things going.

00:15:52.260 --> 00:15:53.720
I see.

00:15:56.480 --> 00:16:00.190
Why did a missile explode at a space base?

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:02.520
Because of the engine fuel?

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:03.350
No.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:04.530
Huh?

00:16:04.530 --> 00:16:07.990
Why were they test launching missiles?

00:16:07.990 --> 00:16:12.780
Don't you know the reason
rockets are being developed?

00:16:12.780 --> 00:16:15.370
To fly to space, right?

00:16:15.370 --> 00:16:18.750
No, for weapons of war.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:26.050
Instead of firing nuclear warheads
at the UK, we'll launch people into space.

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:30.970
The first human spaceflight...
is the first human missile.

00:16:33.510 --> 00:16:37.060
Just kidding. I hope
rockets are being made

00:16:37.060 --> 00:16:40.350
for the sole purpose of going to space.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:43.690
Is that how the future will be?

00:16:43.690 --> 00:16:46.030
In an ideal world.

00:16:50.240 --> 00:16:55.540
Just after the war ended,
my elementary school teacher told me:

00:16:55.540 --> 00:17:00.710
"Planes are for soaring the sky,
not weapons for killing people."

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:05.340
But the next day, she was taken
by the Delivery Crew--

00:17:05.340 --> 00:17:08.630
the Committee for State Security.

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:19.060
Sensei!

00:17:25.270 --> 00:17:27.280
That's all it took.

00:17:27.280 --> 00:17:33.240
She was treated like an enemy
of the state for telling the truth.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:34.570
That's awful.

00:17:36.700 --> 00:17:41.080
I hope she's alive, somewhere out there.

00:17:42.870 --> 00:17:47.420
That's enough of the past.
Let's get back to training.

00:17:52.840 --> 00:17:55.840
November 1st 3:07 AM

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:57.680
With just one month
till launch in December,

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:02.560
we took Irina's parachute
training to the next level.

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:09.280
I'll take care of everything
this time, so just relax!

00:18:09.280 --> 00:18:10.400
But...!

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:16.580
Whatever you do, stay calm. If we get
tied up, we might fall to our deaths.

00:18:16.580 --> 00:18:18.790
Quit scaring me!

00:18:20.450 --> 00:18:21.870
Get ready!

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:29.050
Three! Two! One! Zero!

00:18:32.550 --> 00:18:36.300
Don't panic! Open up your arms and legs!

00:18:36.300 --> 00:18:37.930
L-Like this?!

00:18:37.930 --> 00:18:39.970
Yeah! That's it!

00:18:43.690 --> 00:18:46.810
It's hard to breathe!

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:53.780
Hurry! Our parachute!

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:08.170
Stay focused. There's a lot
to remember to land safely.

00:19:20.220 --> 00:19:25.310
You okay? The first time
is a sensory overload.

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.100
That's enough for--

00:19:26.100 --> 00:19:27.690
Let's go again.

00:19:27.690 --> 00:19:28.770
Huh?

00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:33.650
There's time till sunrise.
Let's go while it's fresh in my memory.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.490
O-Okay.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:41.280
November 2nd 10:21 PM

00:19:41.080 --> 00:19:45.410
She sure is something.
I'm honestly impressed.

00:19:41.280 --> 00:19:42.950
Training Center - Hot Room

00:19:45.410 --> 00:19:50.250
She puts up with everything
the vice-director throws at her.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:51.250
Hey, Franz.

00:19:51.250 --> 00:19:52.250
Hmm?

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:55.420
Why do you think she pushes so hard?

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.090
What?

00:19:57.090 --> 00:20:00.550
It'd make sense if she were a candidate.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:07.850
Love for the motherland, a soldier's
honor... We all have reasons we applied.

00:20:07.850 --> 00:20:12.110
There're people who
just wanted to fly, too.

00:20:12.110 --> 00:20:15.400
I'm not a candidate anymore.

00:20:15.400 --> 00:20:22.160
But she's different. Why does she do it?
Why does she push so hard?

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:25.290
Maybe you shouldn't try to understand.

00:20:25.290 --> 00:20:26.540
Huh?

00:20:26.540 --> 00:20:32.000
Lev, it feels like you're getting
too attached to the subject.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.840
Well...

00:20:33.840 --> 00:20:38.510
Careful. If you develop feelings
for her, it'll only get harder.

00:20:39.630 --> 00:20:40.890
Yeah.

00:20:43.810 --> 00:20:47.890
Almost there... Almost there...!

00:21:42.530 --> 00:21:43.950
I won't lose.

00:21:48.580 --> 00:21:53.420
I won't lose. Not even if I die.

00:21:56.630 --> 00:22:00.720
I... won't lose!

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:51.030
Next Episode:
'A Promise by the Lake'
